  "question": "Should implementation begin on the bounded recovery that restores a trustworthy Claude, Codex, and Pi live signal before one CI confirmation?",
  "summary": "Approve implementation. Independent staff review confirms that all nine current failures are classified from retained evidence: five impossible-state gate failures and Codex keep-moving are stale oracles; Claude Opus recorded lifecycle is a cwd-sensitive harness extraction defect; Codex rejection flow is a lifecycle-invalid fixture; and Pi recorded lifecycle is a real conduct defect because its review never reaches the root assistant channel. The repair preserves every approved journey and changes 12 existing files, estimated at +167/-49 handwritten lines with no generated or golden churn. It must stop for re-approval above 14 files or 292 changed lines. The Pi correction changes only semantic channel and ordering, never prescribed wording, commands, recommendations, or decisions. Focused host tests run first; then the complete local Sonnet, Opus, Codex, and Pi suites must all pass from the same tip before a single full CI run. No scenario withdrawal, prompt coaching, quarantine, compatibility layer, new standing harness, or CI-led iteration is allowed. Staff review completed three correction cycles and now recommends approval with no material, deferred, or polish findings.",
